{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01XEGFwAMY9ZwhfBVqsXcMKH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`ai-engineering/answers/06-006-transformers-why-foundational.md`** — the answer note for Q6: *Transformers — why foundational? ⭐*\n\nKey content in the note:\n- **Concept**: Three simultaneous properties no prior architecture had — fully parallel training, global context via O(1)-hop self-attention, and predictable power-law scaling\n- **Mechanism**: Scaled dot-product attention formula, multi-head specialization, RoPE positional encoding, FFN-as-key-value-memory (Geva 2021), Kaplan scaling laws + Chinchilla 20-token/param optimal ratio\n- **Cross-modal generality**: ViT (images), Whisper (audio), AlphaFold (proteins) — same architecture, different tokenization\n- **Production tradeoff**: O(n²) attention cost → FlashAttention IO-aware tiling as the engineering fix enabling 128K+ context windows\n- **Where transformers lose**: tabular data (GBMs win), truly streaming edge inference, very small datasets\n- Three concrete related question cross-links into category 01-llm-fundamentals"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":69157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cec75431-266a-466c-9a36-b3c5282b0a66","uuid":"a48422fc-a909-48fe-aaab-654e5f6c113b"}
